## The Fire

::bg{location="camp" time="night"}
::music{action="change" mood="peaceful" volume="down"}
<match on="run.night">
  <when is="..1">
    @narrator{code="0010"}: The first night out of Ostwick. The wagons circle, the mules complain, and somebody burns the beans.
  </when>
  <when is="2">
    @narrator{code="0020"}: The mill green at Harrow's Ford. The Marrow folk watch the Company fires from behind their shutters.
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @narrator{code="0030"}: The {{run.night:ordinalWord}} night, within sight of the Tollbridge. Nobody sings.
  </otherwise>
</match>
@narrator{code="0040" when="count('inParty', ['_']) <= 1"}: The fire is too big for the people left around it.
@narrator{code="0050" when="count('inParty', ['_']) >= 3"}: Three companions, one fire, and at least four opinions about everything.
